the 1999 film galaxy quest is a terrific  and clever sci-fi comedy that's both a  satire and a loving tribute to space  sci-fi  there's plenty for both kids and adults  to enjoy about the film but the  hilarious intergalactic romp includes a  lot of jokes and meta commentary that  only adults will appreciate  while galaxy quest is a lighthearted  comedy its sci-fi world is treated as  seriously as it would be in a legitimate  star trek movie  the design and production values are on  par with other big screen  space adventures of its day and similar  talent and methods were employed to make  it that way  the visual effects and starship models  were created by industrial light and  magic  the top shelf effects house that was  born from the production of star wars  the makeup effects for the villainous  series and his soldiers were headed up  by stan winston  the legendary artist behind the thing  according to never surrender a galaxy  quest documentary making the sci-fi  elements the straight man of the comedy  was a deliberate decision  in order for the film to work the sci-fi  stakes needed to be totally real with  the comedic elements stemming from the  human characters or the way the  thermians literally incorporated the  galaxy quest tv show into their culture  making a clear delineation between the  real dangers of space  and the very fake tv world to which the  actors are accustomed actually helped  heighten the comedy  it's the context of the creatures and  circumstances the characters encounter  that makes them funny  not those things themselves  galaxy quest centers around the strained  dynamic between star jason nesmoth and  the rest of the cast of the galaxy quest  tv series which is similar to the  decades-long conflict between star trek  william shatner and his co-stars  much of the cast of star trek have  openly criticized or expressed dislike  for shatner  while shatner expressed puzzlement as to  why castmates leonard nimoy and george  takei  have complained that shatner would use  his power as number one on the show's  call sheet to steal  other actors lines or close-ups or to  try and hog press attention  like nsmith shatner doesn't seem to find  anything wrong with his own behavior but  while jason seems to harbor no ill  will towards the crew shatner is  famously defensive and publicly casts  decay as  irrational however the rest of the trek  cast has enjoyed a very close  family-like relationship much like the  one seen in galaxy quest  in the film gwen demarco says you see we  work together  or not at all this mirrors leonard  nimoy's refusal to participate in star  trek the animated series unless michelle  nichols and george takei were also hired  nichols and walter koenig were best lady  and best man  at takei's wedding to which shatner was  not invited shatner also did not attend  leonard nimoy's funeral due to a  scheduling conflict but says he  doesn't think he'd have been welcome  anyway in galaxy quest alan rickman's  character alexander  dain is a serious actor who feels that  his career has been destroyed by his  years playing the alien dr lazarus  dane's plight is far from uncommon as  actors who do sci-fi television often  find themselves shoehorned into similar  roles  but alexander's frustration seemed to be  particularly inspired by the life of one  particular trek cast member  leonard nimoy while nimoy might not have  expressed the levels of resentment that  dane does in the film  he did struggle with being so closely  identified with spock  nimoy found that it made it hard to  further his career as an actor  leading to his moving behind the camera  as a director  this struggle became exaggerated in the  public eye when his first autobiography  was published under the controversial  title i am not spock  which created a misconception that nimoy  disliked the role  and the place it created for him in pop  culture nimoy sought to correct this  perception by naming his 1995 follow-up  i am spock while dane's story is more  dramatic he  also makes peace with his iconic role by  the end of the film  one of galaxy quest's running gags is  the quiet calm of fred quan who doesn't  seem to respond appropriately to any of  the peril and weirdness that happens  throughout the film  it's easy to read the chill frequently  snacking fred as being in a  marijuana-fueled haze throughout the  action  this is actually deliberate and is a  holdover from the original intent that  galaxy quest be a more adult-oriented  comedy  tony shalhoub was originally up for the  part of gai which ultimately went to sam  rockwell but director dean pariso  invited shaloub to play fred kwan  instead  shalub initially declined as he felt an  asian actor should play an asian  character but the two determined that  fred himself is actually a non-asian  actor playing the asian character  tech sergeant chen this development  reminded shaloub of an unconfirmed rumor  that actor david carradine while  portraying the whitewashed role of kwai  chang kane on the 1970's tv series kung  fu  smoked weed constantly on set shalub and  pariso invented a backstory for fred  that he had done the same thing  and then ended up becoming a burnout and  the part was totally  rewritten with that in mind very little  of this made it into the final film with  many of chalub's stoner gags being cut  and the only acknowledgement of fred's  faking his ethnicity being a passing  reference to kwon not  really being his last name early in  galaxy quest we learned that jason  nezmuth has been hired to make  a personal appearance by teenage fan  brandon and his friends  jason explains it by saying it's not a  big deal these guys put a little set in  their basement i'm there about an hour  however despite jason's downplaying  consider how expensive it must be  to book jason nesmoth for a one hour  appearance  yes he's an out of work actor but he's  still got a nice house in the hollywood  hills and  is apparently in enough demand to  warrant a three-day convention dedicated  to his long-cancelled tv series  serious acting work may have dried up  but there's no shortage of people  looking to pay money for nsmith's  attention  in 2021 a 10-minute live zoom call with  star trek actor jonathan frakes  cost 750 getting galaxy quest's  lead actor to play his most famous role  for an hour in their basement could not  be cheap  even if you skimp on the limo after  receiving and misinterpreting earth's  television broadcast  the thermians remodeled their entire  society and technology after galaxy  quest  in excruciating detail while earth's tv  signals really do escape our planet and  travel into space  when you do the math the thermian's  galaxy quest makeover must have been  extremely rapid  let's be generous and imagine that  thermia is a very close neighbor to  earth  the closest star to our sun proxima  centauri actually does have a planet  proxima b  proxima is about 4.2 light years from  earth so it would take a television  broadcast 4.2 years to reach there  galaxy quest aired roughly between 1977  and 1982 so its first episodes would  have reached proxima beginning in the  early 1980s  the film is set less than two decades  later in 1999 or 2000.  if the thermians lived on proxima b that  doesn't leave very long to reconstruct  their culture develop their technology  to mimic that of galaxy quest and then  travel all the way to earth and if you  consider thermia  is probably much farther away that gives  them even less time to work with  it's obvious when watching the film that  thermians are scientifically brilliant  but factoring for real-life physical  constraints their genius is actually  understated  when we last see the thermians in galaxy  quest math czar  is commanding the nsea protector with a  newfound confidence and the ship  warps off into space after dropping off  the television cast back on earth  but as light and positive as this scene  is framed and as cheerful as the  thermians seem their future is actually  looking pretty bleak  as teb reveals earlier in the film the  crew of the protector  is all that remains of the thermian  civilization  after the rest were exterminated by  general serris  aside from the protector's starport  mathazar and his crew have no home to  which to return  being forced to wander the stars  indefinitely in their starship is  definitely  preferable to extermination but it will  still be a struggle  plus the crew will also eventually have  to cope with the recent demise of their  homeworld  the film's finale sees the human cast of  galaxy quest crash landing the command  deck of the nsea protector into the main  stage of the galaxy quest convention  the fans inside the hall seem to think  this is just an elaborate stunt but the  moment they leave the building they're  going to notice that there's a path of  destruction  running through the parking lot and a  gaping hole in the side of the building  some other cars have been destroyed  people are going to put two and two  together  the very last minute of the film reveals  that following the events of the film  galaxy quest returns to television for  new episodes  but somewhere in between there would  have to have been  some consequences of an alien spaceship  crash landing into a california civic  center  did the u.s government get involved was  there a cover-up  how did they keep people from talking  one possible explanation could be that  in exchange for their silence a shady  government entity  offered the hundreds of witnesses at the  convention the one thing they wanted  most  the return of the cheesy tv show they  love  part of what keeps the stakes of galaxy  quest pretty light is that there are no  negative consequences of the actors  being abducted by aliens near the start  of the film  when gwen and the crew tell jason that  they want to go home  jason pushes back by implying there's  nothing waiting for them there  say the word we'll go home pay our bills  feed our fish  fall asleep in front of the tv and miss  out on all of  this this is a sad realization about the  characters but it's very convenient for  the story  none of the cast has partners waiting  for them to come home or kids who need  to be picked up from soccer practice  no one tries to get in touch with anyone  back on earth at least not until jason  needs to reach brandon for some tech  support  the galaxy quest cast is evidently the  only family any of them have which  ratchets up the importance of their  relationship  and makes their ability to get along the  highest personal stakes for these  characters  galaxy quest is a breezy comedy  adventure but it's also a story about  how investing emotionally in a fictional  world can enrich your real life  the thermians found peace and purpose in  literally believing in  idolized heroes the show's fans too  clearly find a lot of enrichment in  knowingly participating in the fantasy  of galaxy quest  both groups provide a lot of unwitting  humor in the film but that humor is  mostly good-natured  while both the human and  extraterrestrial fans of the galaxy  quest tv series have  already learned the importance of  fantasy before the start of the story  it takes the main characters of the  series a little longer over the course  of the film we see the jaded and  exhausted actors  slowly become the heroes that their fans  always believed them to be  jason only truly becomes the commander  once he puts his trust in his friends  and comes clean to the thermians about  his deception alexander finds dr lazarus  within himself by understanding what he  means to quellic who sees him as a  surrogate father  fred tommy and guy each find a new  confidence by rising to the standards of  their characters and beyond the cast  grows through the belief of people who  look at them  and see the people they'd like to be  even if they weren't real to begin with  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

